  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything. Removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` breaks a rule in this repo.\n\n- **Event (ARCH-4):** `OrderPlaced` (`src/core/events.ts:16`, schema v3) is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repos. Removing a field is a breaking change for deployed consumers. It has to go through deprecation. \"Nothing in this repo reads it\" doesn't show that those two services don't.\n- **API (ARCH-8):** `channel` is a required field on `POST /orders`. It is validated in `src/core/order.ts:124` and parsed in `src/api/requestParsing.ts:18`. I haven't checked whether `GET /orders/{id}` returns it. If it does, web-storefront may depend on it, and removing it would break that too.\n\nDropping it from the order model would also take it out of the event, since the event is built from the model.\n\nI can do either of these:\n\n1. **Deprecate, don't remove.**\n   - Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in `OrderPlaced`.\n   - Make it optional on `POST /orders` and stop validating it.\n   - Keep publishing it, using a fixed default when it's absent.\n   - Once billing-service and analytics-ingest confirm they don't use it, remove it in a follow-up with a schema version bump.\n2. **Remove it everywhere now.** Do this only if you can confirm both consumers (and web-storefront, if the GET response includes it) don't use it, and that you accept the schema change. Tell me and I'll make the change and update the tests and README.\n\nWhich do you want?",
